  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nSo [\\<template for\\> and processing instructions](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#the-template-element:~:text=The%20for%20content%20attribute) are a relatively recent addition to the standard. They work in recent Chrome too. However, these are quite limited, as they only allow inserting literal elements into the DOM, without any parametrization. So it’s impossible to somehow insert some content on the call / insertion site, which makes these inferior to any templating system (even Mustache.)\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\nNone that I know of. No way to insert things into processing instructions.\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\n`<slot>` has been there for an eternity, especially as part of `<template>`. So it is kinda intuitive that `<slot>` is a good compatible approach to `<template>` & processing instructions.\n\n### Anything else?\n\n_No response_",
